{"id": "EUVD-2026-102278", "enisaUuid": "dee16368-6724-3e7e-99f7-d2edbe0b53cf", "description": "OpenJPH through 0.32.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the HTJ2K cleanup-pass decoder that allows attackers to corrupt memory via one-row codeblocks. Attackers can supply a crafted .j2c or .jph codestream with small precinct sizes, causing the decoder to write a second row past the codeblock buffer, resulting in memory corruption and crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:36:21", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/openjph-htj2k-degenerate-codeblock-cleanup-oob-write", "https://github.com/aous72/OpenJPH/blob/23c422895ce6c3a156935222e4715ee0b7be952c/src/core/codestream/ojph_subband.cpp#L136-L142", "https://github.com/aous72/OpenJPH/blob/23c422895ce6c3a156935222e4715ee0b7be952c/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp#L79-L84", "https://github.com/aous72/OpenJPH/blob/23c422895ce6c3a156935222e4715ee0b7be952c/src/core/coding/ojph_block_decoder32.cpp#L1135-L1155", "https://github.com/aous72/OpenJPH", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openjph-through-0.32.0-heap-out-of-bounds-write-in-htj2k-cleanup-pass-decoder"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5g7q-q9vm-h587", "CVE-2026-111151"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8d0c7df2-8614-314b-8b22-5a3253b93ce6", "product": {"name": "OpenJPH", "vendor": {"name": "aous72"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "54355fb8-8141-3f71-982d-a9faedeec223", "vendor": {"name": "aous72"}}], "isExploited": false}